cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "pi-tape: record, replay and fork an agent session"
abstract: >-
  pi-tape records a pi agent session to a compact, redactable tape and replays it
  deterministically: recorded answers are served instead of calling a provider, and
  recorded tool calls are replaced instead of being run again. Requests are keyed by a
  prefix hash, which makes a fork possible — serve the recording while the context
  matches, ask a real model where it does not. A second layer derives checkable
  procedures from several recordings of the same task.
authors:
